**Technical Assessment: TurboFieldfare**

TurboFieldfare is a specialized inference runtime for the Gemma 4 26B-A4B model on Apple Silicon, designed to fit within an 8 GB RAM constraint. The central resource bottleneck is memory bandwidth and capacity; the system cannot hold the full 14.3 GB model in RAM. Instead, it maintains a ~2 GB footprint by keeping the shared core and KV cache resident while streaming expert weights from SSD on demand.

The architecture divides data into two tiers. Resident data includes the shared expert weights and the KV cache, which remain in Metal-visible memory.